[Rhys Sullivan's practical guide](https://x.com/RhysSullivan/status/2103280866084708510) starts with the jobs people already do in a product. It asks MCP authors to expose dashboard actions, keep code mode as a choice made by the agent's client, and provide documentation search. It also covers links to specific product actions, groups of tools, and OAuth authorization.
OAuth lets a person authorize a client to access a service.

The table compares his advice with rat-stack today. The gaps remain open; this page authorizes no changes.

| Rhys's point | rat-stack today | Verdict |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Do what the dashboard can do. | Each interface uses the same contract and handler. The public site exposes `search` and `read`; the CLI projects registered capabilities too. | Agree |
| Keep code mode out of the default MCP tool list. | CLI `mcp` uses plain tools; `--code-mode` opts into code mode. The hosted site's MCP includes `execute` because demonstrating the sandbox is the site's job. | Agree in the template; the hosted site differs |
| Ship search for docs and skills. | The site's `search` and `read` capabilities cover public content. Lore pages are included in the searchable documentation. | Agree |
| Add a deep link into the product. | No product-action deep-link tool appears in the hosted capability registry. | Gap |
| Offer toolsets and permissions tied to the auth token. | Contracts can require approval, and `Approval` gates execution. The hosted MCP has no user-token toolsets; `auth.md` says it accepts no credentials. | Gap |
| Let clients use OAuth; an API spec and Client ID Metadata Document (CIMD) OAuth cover most agents. | The auth cartridge supports Better Auth sessions for an app, but ratstack.sh says it has no OAuth or access tokens. | Gap |

The comparison uses `apps/mischief/src/capabilities/index.ts`, `apps/cli/src/command.ts`, `packages/capability/src/approval.ts`, `packages/auth/src/auth.ts`, and the hosted site's `auth.md`. See [one capability, every surface](/lore/one-capability-every-surface) and the [cartridges](/lore/cartridges) page for the contracts and auth boundary.
